From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:44:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] scripts: read the IMU without evdev, numpy or a GUI

display_imu.py imports evdev, numpy, the cube renderer and the uinput
mouse before it parses its arguments, so capturing samples for a
calibration pulls in Qt, OpenGL, trimesh and scipy, none of which a
headless box has any use for. Read the event device with the struct
module, keep the little vector arithmetic in plain Python, and import
numpy, ahrs, draw_cube and uinput_mouse only in the branches that use
them, so that --csv needs nothing beyond the standard library. Add
--seconds so a capture can end on its own over a serial console or ssh.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
